# Public client-side configuration for atrium-web.
#
# atrium is web-only (ADR-001): a static, scroll-driven index of the six
# showcase projects, read from a typed in-repo data module. There is NO
# backend and NO network at runtime, so only the two optional public
# variables below exist. Both have documented placeholder fallbacks, so
# the build is correct even before a real deploy / a git remote exists.
#
# Never commit a real `.env` (CLAUDE.md § 4) — this `.env.example` is the
# only committed env file.

# Canonical public origin for absolute URLs — drives `metadataBase`, the
# canonical <link>, the OG/Twitter image URL, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, and the
# JSON-LD `@id`/`url`. Unset, it falls back to the documented placeholder
# `https://atrium-demo.fly.dev` (see src/lib/site-config.ts). The production
# deploy bakes this at build time (the bare `atrium` Fly name was taken, so the
# app is `atrium-demo`). Set this to the real origin if hosting elsewhere (the
# eventual portfolio root domain). A trailing slash is stripped automatically.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://atrium-demo.fly.dev

# Base GitHub URL for the six per-project repo links. A git remote now exists
# (github.com/AntczakJ/portfolio), but the repo is still PRIVATE and `main` is
# not fully pushed, so this stays unset and the repo affordances render as
# disabled "coming soon" controls (ADR-003 / U2) — a live link would 404 for
# visitors. Once the repo is public and pushed, set this to the real owner/repo
# base and every repo link becomes a live monorepo deep-link with no other code
# change.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_BASE=https://github.com/AntczakJ/portfolio
